WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Alice: Alright everyone, let's kick off the weekly sync. Bob, do you want to start with the backend updates?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.200
Bob: Sure. This week we finally merged the PR for the new caching layer. The latency on the dashboard API dropped by almost 40%. It's looking really stable.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.100
Charlie: That's great news, Bob. I did notice a small spike in memory usage on the Redis cluster though. Have we looked into that?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Bob: I checked Datadog this morning. It looks like it was temporary during the cache warming phase, but I will monitor it for the next 48 hours.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:40.000
Alice: Good catch, Charlie. Bob, could you create an action item to investigate the memory spike just in case? If there are any leaks, we need them patched before the 2.0 release on Friday.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.500
Bob: Will do. Regarding the Friday release, are we completely locked feature-wise?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:58.200
Charlie: Almost. The UI team is just fixing a couple of alignment bugs on the settings page, but functionally we are fully code complete. Alice, can you review the release notes today?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.500
Alice: Yes, I'll review and approve the release notes by EOD. Is there anything else blocking us?

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Bob: None on my end. Backend is solid.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.000
Charlie: Same here. Frontend is ready for the freeze.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Alice: Excellent. Let's touch base again on Wednesday to double-check the staging environment. Great work this week, team. Let's wrap it up early.
